1
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:09,384
[birds chirping]

2
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:12,054
[♪ Forever Loving You ♪
by Nora Aunor playing]

3
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:27,152
♪ Why did I ever say goodbye? ♪

4
00:00:27,236 --> 00:00:32,908
♪ Why did I ever make you cry? ♪

5
00:00:33,617 --> 00:00:39,623
♪ When all the while
I knew you cared ♪

6
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:45,629
♪ And love's just starting
To be real ♪

7
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:51,969
♪ I blame myself for losing you ♪

8
00:00:52,261 --> 00:00:57,724
♪ I was a fool to let you go ♪

9
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:04,189
♪ My restless night has found me so ♪

10
00:01:04,356 --> 00:01:09,236
♪ Come back once more, I beg of you ♪

11
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:15,200
♪ Regrets fill my heart,
Now I need you ♪

12
00:01:15,284 --> 00:01:21,331
♪ I'm longing to start life anew ♪

13
00:01:21,415 --> 00:01:26,920
♪ Forgive and forget,
Now I'm learning ♪

14
00:01:27,004 --> 00:01:34,344
♪ And I'll try
Not to hurt you again ♪

15
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:40,517
♪ And after all the things
I've done ♪

16
00:01:40,601 --> 00:01:45,939
♪ I've known that there is only one ♪

17
00:01:46,732 --> 00:01:52,654
♪ My roving days and nights
Are through ♪

18
00:01:52,738 --> 00:01:58,327
♪ I'll stay forevеr loving you ♪

19
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:06,835
♪ I'll stay forevеr loving you ♪

20
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:10,797
WHAT'S MINE IS YOURS

21
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,216
WHAT'S THE TEA?
WITH OGIE DIAZ

22
00:02:13,467 --> 00:02:15,302
What a shocker!

23
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:17,054
What is this, huh?

24
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:19,181
- [camera shutter clicks]
- [crowd cheering]

25
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:21,558
[thrilling music]

26
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:25,646
They say it's a star-studded list.

27
00:02:29,483 --> 00:02:32,027
Of course,
it's a red-carpet premiere.

28
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:35,072
First on this list
of confirmed attendees

29
00:02:35,489 --> 00:02:38,825
is this power couple
which we'll refer to

30
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:40,827
as "The Lady and the Champ."

31
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:42,037
Ooh...

32
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,747
You can't miss this!

33
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:48,293
Look out for these stars
who are said to arrive too.

34
00:02:48,377 --> 00:02:50,629
Super and Duper.

35
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,381
Ooh!

36
00:02:52,464 --> 00:02:53,590
Slay! [gasps]

37
00:02:53,674 --> 00:02:55,175
But wait, there's more!

38
00:02:55,258 --> 00:02:58,553
This kid is definitely showing up.

39
00:02:58,637 --> 00:03:00,180
The Comeback Kid.

40
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:02,557
And this is indeed a comeback!

41
00:03:02,641 --> 00:03:06,812
A star-studded reunion like this
is a rare event, I tell you!

42
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:09,648
It's crazy,
it's like a meteor shower!

43
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:12,067
So stay tuned, my tea-loving friends.

44
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:15,779
Because whenever
there's a meteor shower

45
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:19,116
you can expect a big bang!

46
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,992
[laughs]

47
00:03:21,076 --> 00:03:23,120
[coughs]

48
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:24,621
WHAT'S THE TEA?
WITH OGIE DIAZ

49
00:03:25,122 --> 00:03:27,124
[theme music]

50
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:30,836
♪ Careful, careful ♪

51
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,798
♪ The world is full
Of jealous people ♪

52
00:03:34,881 --> 00:03:38,009
♪ When envy strikes,
It means trouble♪

53
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:40,220
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

54
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:42,347
♪ Careful, careful ♪

55
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:46,351
♪ We always need to be careful ♪

56
00:03:46,852 --> 00:03:49,312
♪ Prying eyes ready to snoop ♪

57
00:03:49,396 --> 00:03:52,524
♪ Digging for the juiciest scoop ♪

58
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:55,110
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

59
00:03:58,405 --> 00:04:00,615
♪ Careful, careful ♪

60
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:19,342
This looks good.

61
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:22,512
Um, can you deliver
to the office by 6 p.m.?

62
00:04:22,763 --> 00:04:24,389
Yes, ma'am,
we'll make this a rush order.

63
00:04:24,765 --> 00:04:27,017
- [Andrea] Thank you.
- My condolences.

64
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:29,144
Thanks.

65
00:04:44,034 --> 00:04:45,035
I'll take these too.

66
00:04:45,869 --> 00:04:48,622
- [Andrea] Can you deliver this now?
- [vendor] Sure, ma'am!

67
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:50,832
- Those are freshly made.
- [Andrea] Thanks.

68
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:53,710
[dramatic music]

69
00:05:02,469 --> 00:05:03,887
[Samuel in English]
We've come far, Matthew.

70
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:05,639
[in Filipino] SAM would not be SAM

71
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:07,766
if I didn't convince you to join me.

72
00:05:09,476 --> 00:05:11,019
I want you to know that

73
00:05:11,478 --> 00:05:13,897
it's you that I trust the most.

74
00:05:14,523 --> 00:05:17,359
Don't make any decisions
until I get back.

75
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:20,695
[dramatic music continues]

76
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:36,294
[dramatic music fades]

77
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:42,342
[Gina in English]
Matthew, your coffee's ready.

78
00:05:46,096 --> 00:05:47,222
Shoot, I'm late.

79
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,600
[in Filipino]
I'm sure they'll understand

80
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:51,685
why you're late.

81
00:05:52,227 --> 00:05:53,478
[in English] Especially Samuel.

82
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,314
But it's so tragic.

83
00:05:57,566 --> 00:05:58,733
[in Filipino] I didn't know

84
00:05:58,817 --> 00:06:00,819
Samuel was buried in debt!

85
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,906
But still, that's not a good reason
to kill himself.

86
00:06:06,575 --> 00:06:07,993
[in English]
He died of a heart attack.

87
00:06:08,243 --> 00:06:09,494
[in Filipino]
I already told you, Gina.

88
00:06:09,578 --> 00:06:10,954
But I saw it right here!

89
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:12,414
Oh!

90
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:13,999
It's a blind item!

91
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:19,629
[Matthew] This was written by idiots.

92
00:06:19,713 --> 00:06:21,965
I'll tell you if he killed himself.

93
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:23,383
[in English] I'm not so sure.

94
00:06:24,968 --> 00:06:25,969
[in Filipino] I know you.

95
00:06:27,012 --> 00:06:29,139
You have a lot of secrets.

96
00:06:30,891 --> 00:06:31,892
[Gina chuckles]

97
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:36,021
Wait.

98
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:40,150
Did you ever tell Samuel
about Paul Amir's offer?

99
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,277
No.

100
00:06:43,028 --> 00:06:44,029
Nobody knows.

101
00:06:45,405 --> 00:06:46,781
[in English]
Actually, it's just an offer.

102
00:06:47,157 --> 00:06:48,199
Nothing's final.

103
00:06:49,451 --> 00:06:50,994
[in Filipino]
I guess it's for the best.

104
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:53,622
It would have hurt Samuel.

105
00:06:53,705 --> 00:06:56,541
Maybe you don't have to leave SAM.

106
00:06:57,375 --> 00:06:58,418
What do you mean?

107
00:06:59,044 --> 00:07:00,670
[in English] Well, Samuel is gone.

108
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:04,883
And SAM cannot continue
without a leader.

109
00:07:06,426 --> 00:07:08,845
[Gina in Filipino]
Which one of you will take his place?

110
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:12,140
[in English]
And who deserves it the most?

111
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:15,769
[Samuel in Filipino]
I've tried everything.

112
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:19,481
I put up a business,
I went into sales.

113
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:22,067
But I was never really into it.

114
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:27,072
I became a producer too,
but it was too difficult.

115
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:30,951
And I never really made it
as an actor.

116
00:07:32,953 --> 00:07:34,537
But when I became a manager

117
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:36,623
I was happy.

118
00:07:37,332 --> 00:07:39,417
It was something else, believe me.

119
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:40,961
[exclaims]

120
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:43,463
Hey, that's not allowed here.

121
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:44,881
[clatters]

122
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:49,678
Take all of these upstairs.

123
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:53,264
Careful.

124
00:07:53,556 --> 00:07:55,558
[thrilling music]

125
00:08:01,106 --> 00:08:02,148
[Camille] Yes, sir.

126
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,192
Yes, you may leave the flowers

127
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,903
at the reception area.

128
00:08:07,654 --> 00:08:09,614
Yes, you can come visit any time.

129
00:08:13,076 --> 00:08:15,370
[thrilling music continues]

130
00:08:15,453 --> 00:08:16,997
- Good morning, Dad.
- [Matthew] Good morning.

131
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:28,258
Morning, Dad.

132
00:08:29,718 --> 00:08:30,719
Camille?

133
00:08:32,262 --> 00:08:33,304
Sir?

134
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:35,140
Do you need me to call Camille?

135
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,977
[exhales sharply]

136
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:49,237
What's going on downstairs?

137
00:08:50,864 --> 00:08:52,073
Memorial service.

138
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:54,868
[Matthew] Here?

139
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:58,204
It's Mother Aleta's idea.

140
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:01,750
It's for industry colleagues.

141
00:09:01,833 --> 00:09:03,168
[Gab] Sofie's making the calls
to them.

142
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:05,128
[Andrea] It's okay.
At least it's private.

143
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:08,214
If anywhere else
and our talents show up

144
00:09:08,298 --> 00:09:09,924
so will their fans.

145
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:11,843
It will be chaotic.

146
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:14,512
It's embarrassing
and Samuel's wife wouldn't like it.

147
00:09:14,596 --> 00:09:17,348
Helen is coming here?

148
00:09:17,682 --> 00:09:18,725
[Andrea] I don't know.

149
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:20,435
How will we get any work done today?

150
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:21,895
What's your problem?

151
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:24,189
Mother Aleta's taking care of it.

152
00:09:25,148 --> 00:09:26,191
Look.

153
00:09:27,484 --> 00:09:29,694
We haven't really
talked about it, but...

154
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:32,739
what will we do
about Samuel's talents?

155
00:09:33,073 --> 00:09:34,199
[Matthew] How do we split them up?

156
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,242
Wow.

157
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:38,369
I seriously don't know.

158
00:09:38,453 --> 00:09:40,789
[in English] I just think that
we should come out with a statement.

159
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:43,083
A "moving forward" statement.

160
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:44,292
You know what, Matt?

161
00:09:45,627 --> 00:09:49,422
[in Filipino] Samuel's body
hasn't even arrived from Germany

162
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:53,426
and we're already
splitting his talents?

163
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:56,304
[in English] Don't you think we have
to find a perfect time for this

164
00:09:56,387 --> 00:09:58,139
- and not tonight?
- [Matthew in Filipino] Then when?

165
00:09:58,223 --> 00:10:00,683
What if Samuel's talents leave us?

166
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:04,646
Why would they do that?

167
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:06,856
[in English] Come on, Gabriel.

168
00:10:07,357 --> 00:10:09,150
You think they're here because of us?

169
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,487
The only reason they're here

170
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:15,657
is because being managed
by Samuel Mendiola is a big deal.

171
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,408
The ultimate star-maker.

172
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:20,787
Look, now that he's gone...

173
00:10:24,499 --> 00:10:25,542
You know, I...

174
00:10:27,252 --> 00:10:29,629
I love Samuel
just as much as the two of you.

175
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:33,216
But knowing him,
I mean, he would want to see

176
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:35,593
that SAM is running smoothly
even without him.

177
00:10:35,927 --> 00:10:36,970
For example...

178
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:40,974
[in Filipino] You think he'd be happy
you passed up on Kiray's big break?

179
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:42,058
[scoffs]

180
00:10:43,393 --> 00:10:44,894
[in English]
I told you, I'm handling it.

181
00:10:44,978 --> 00:10:46,771
[scoffs] How?

182
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:48,857
[Andrea] Can you just
leave him alone?

183
00:10:49,691 --> 00:10:50,692
Matty.

184
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:54,487
[in Filipino] I don't have
to update you about my talents.

185
00:10:54,571 --> 00:10:55,697
Then who will you update?

186
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,532
- There's only three of us left.
- [Gab sighs]

187
00:10:57,824 --> 00:10:59,826
[Matthew]
We three will have to run SAM now.

188
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,954
How do we do that? No meetings?
No more brainstorming?

189
00:11:03,288 --> 00:11:04,330
Andrea, how?

190
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:05,498
[knocking on door]

191
00:11:05,582 --> 00:11:06,624
[Camille] Excuse me.

192
00:11:07,292 --> 00:11:08,334
Not now, Noemi.

193
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:12,338
Ms. Andrea,
Ms. Maricel is in your office.

194
00:11:12,422 --> 00:11:14,048
There. There's your update.

195
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:16,551
Maricel Soriano is in my office.

196
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:18,011
Happy?

197
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:20,972
[Andrea in English] Let's go.

198
00:11:22,515 --> 00:11:23,516
[door closes]

199
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:25,810
[gasps]

200
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:27,896
[in Filipino] This is it?

201
00:11:27,979 --> 00:11:31,482
This is the great new project
you have for me?

202
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:32,609
[scoffs]

203
00:11:35,278 --> 00:11:36,279
SORIO AND TEKLA, UNDERAGE,
TARAY AND TEROY

204
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:37,363
QUIAPO KID, TAKEN FROM HEAVEN,
SUPER NANNY AND THE GOLDEN DUCK

205
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:38,531
YOUR HAND, PLEASE, TOMORROW IS MINE,
PEPE AND PILAR

206
00:11:41,284 --> 00:11:43,036
This is the best Shine can do for me?

207
00:11:44,579 --> 00:11:45,914
- [Camille] Hi.
- [mumbles]

208
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:47,582
[in English]
What are you talking about?

209
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:51,294
[in Filipino]
A lot of people would kill

210
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:52,629
just to play Paula on this project!

211
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:54,005
And the role is yours!

212
00:11:54,088 --> 00:11:56,216
[in English]
I know and the role fits me well!

213
00:11:56,299 --> 00:11:57,383
- Right?
- [Andrea] Exactly.

214
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:59,636
[in Filipino]
Now, if we had Jodi Sta. Maria

215
00:11:59,719 --> 00:12:00,720
or Eula Valdez in it with me

216
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:02,180
I may reconsider.

217
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:04,766
But Snooky? Oh, my god!

218
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:07,101
She will be the death of that film.

219
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:09,229
You're still mad at Snooky?

220
00:12:09,312 --> 00:12:10,897
After all this time?

221
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:12,273
It's forever.

222
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:14,067
The nerve of that woman!

223
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:17,028
The audacity. How dare she!

224
00:12:18,488 --> 00:12:19,864
Why don't I just...

225
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,408
Why don't I do
that other project instead?

226
00:12:22,951 --> 00:12:24,410
- Juan Makabayan?
- Yes.

227
00:12:24,494 --> 00:12:27,247
Oh, there's nothing in there for you.

228
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:28,539
I read the script.

229
00:12:28,623 --> 00:12:31,501
Of course,
I looked for a perfect role for you.

230
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:33,795
Something that stands out,
but there's nothing.

231
00:12:35,338 --> 00:12:38,424
Maybe I should just let my aunt
manage my career.

232
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:41,386
The accountant or the nurse?

233
00:12:41,803 --> 00:12:42,845
The dentist.

234
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:45,765
Sure, she knows nothing
about managing

235
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:47,725
but at least she cares about me.

236
00:12:48,059 --> 00:12:51,020
I only signed with you
because of Samuel.

237
00:12:51,354 --> 00:12:53,815
Because he promised me
he'd take care of me.

238
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:56,067
That he'd give me
everything I wanted.

239
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:58,319
And most of all,
he promised that Snooky and I

240
00:12:58,403 --> 00:13:01,030
would never, ever be
in the same film again.

241
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:03,950
This is all Samuel's fault!

242
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:06,035
He decided to become
a stupid drug addict at his old age.

243
00:13:06,119 --> 00:13:09,747
I mean, what 70-year-old dies
of a drug overdose?

244
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:11,207
Hey.

245
00:13:11,416 --> 00:13:13,459
Samuel never did drugs.

246
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:15,503
He died of a heart attack.

247
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,588
Oh, did he, really?

248
00:13:17,839 --> 00:13:18,840
[scoffs]

249
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:20,883
Well, whatever.

250
00:13:21,092 --> 00:13:23,761
He's dead, so there's no one
who cares about me anymore.

251
00:13:24,679 --> 00:13:27,598
[Maricel] Maybe I should
switch agencies.

252
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:29,559
Galaxy's there.

253
00:13:30,018 --> 00:13:31,978
Or Aunt Metring might do better.

254
00:13:33,396 --> 00:13:36,274
Ms. Mary,
you don't have to decide now.

255
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:40,069
We can talk some more
when you come back for the memorial.

256
00:13:40,153 --> 00:13:42,572
What makes you think I'm attending?

257
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:45,783
I'm so disrespected here.

258
00:13:45,867 --> 00:13:47,577
Too bad you're not coming

259
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,163
since Director Mac will be there.

260
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,582
[Andrea] He wants to see you
and Snooky.

261
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,584
Just a preliminary meeting...

262
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:55,877
Snooky's coming?

263
00:13:56,169 --> 00:13:58,296
Yes, that's what Gab told me.

264
00:13:58,379 --> 00:14:00,965
She has a lot of ideas
and suggestions for the film

265
00:14:01,049 --> 00:14:03,968
like what to add in her scenes
in the film.

266
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:07,096
- Oh, darn fairy!
- Where's the fairy?

267
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,681
- There.
- Oh, yeah, that's a fairy.

268
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:09,932
Found it.

269
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,559
- Chin?
- [Chin] Oh, I didn't notice you.

270
00:14:11,642 --> 00:14:14,812
I was looking for my contact lens.
Oh, hello, Ms. Mary!

271
00:14:14,896 --> 00:14:17,148
How'd they end up on the floor?

272
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:19,150
They fell out, I don't know.

273
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:22,111
- I'll message you, okay, Mary?
- [Maricel] Yeah.

274
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:24,364
[Chin] Camille, I need your help.
Come with me.

275
00:14:24,781 --> 00:14:26,366
Girl, that is so old news.

276
00:14:26,449 --> 00:14:27,950
You really should know these things.

277
00:14:28,034 --> 00:14:31,996
You're in showbiz now, so keep up!

278
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:33,664
Were we already alive then?

279
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:37,335
Yes, we were in diapers, probably.

280
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:41,422
But anyway,
I'm sure you must have seen

281
00:14:41,506 --> 00:14:42,799
their old movie on TV.

282
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:44,634
It's called What's Mine is Yours.

283
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:49,055
There were rumors that Maricel
was way better in it than Snooky.

284
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:50,848
[Chin] So Maricel
expected all the awards.

285
00:14:50,932 --> 00:14:53,976
But Snooky won them all
like a grand slam.

286
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:56,270
Oh, my god.

287
00:14:56,354 --> 00:15:00,233
And Maricel got nothing,
besides certificates of nomination.

288
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:01,526
For real?

289
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:03,194
Oh, my god, wait! There's more!

290
00:15:03,736 --> 00:15:04,737
Did you know?

291
00:15:05,154 --> 00:15:06,489
Maricel also told the press

292
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:10,284
that Sir Samuel and Snooky
were having an affair!

293
00:15:10,368 --> 00:15:12,662
- That's absolutely correct!
- [gasps]

294
00:15:13,371 --> 00:15:15,415
[Daisy] And get this.

295
00:15:16,249 --> 00:15:20,169
Of course,
Snooky wouldn't stand for it.

296
00:15:20,253 --> 00:15:21,838
She told the press that it was really

297
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:25,675
Maricel having an affair with him!

298
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:27,176
Oh, I heard that!

299
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,595
I'm confused. So which one was it?

300
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:30,972
Girl.

301
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:34,016
Both of them. Among others.

302
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,477
Sir Samuel was such a playboy!

303
00:15:36,561 --> 00:15:38,104
[cackles] And...

304
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:40,898
Even Mother Aleta was one.

305
00:15:40,982 --> 00:15:42,275
- Yeah!
- It's all crazy!

306
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:44,610
- Oh, and by the way...
- [Camille] Wait...

307
00:15:44,986 --> 00:15:48,948
Who was he with
on that "orghi" in Germany?

308
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:50,116
What "orghi"? It's "orjee".

309
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:52,243
[Daisy] It's "orjee"?
They changed it?

310
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:53,661
No, it's always been "orjee".

311
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:54,787
[gasps]

312
00:15:54,871 --> 00:15:58,040
How many people should there be
in an orgy, anyway?

313
00:15:58,124 --> 00:16:00,084
What orgy are you talking about?

314
00:16:00,168 --> 00:16:04,172
I'm talking about the orgy
that killed Sir Sam!

315
00:16:04,255 --> 00:16:06,507
He couldn't handle
all the orgy action

316
00:16:06,591 --> 00:16:08,259
because he was too old.

317
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:10,094
No, you idiot!

318
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:12,889
Sir Samuel died of a heart attack!

319
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:14,056
No, really?

320
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,766
Yes, that's what the doctor said.

321
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:19,270
- Oops! Wrong info.
- Goodness, Miss Daisy!

322
00:16:19,604 --> 00:16:22,732
- I'm so sorry, friends.
- Now she's spread it.

323
00:16:23,024 --> 00:16:24,817
- Fake news...
- Take that back!

324
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:26,903
- It's fake!
- It wasn't an orghi.

325
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,946
- There she goes again.
- Crazy.

326
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:32,575
But anyway, that's why we're here,
doing interior decorating

327
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:34,827
and writing thank-you cards
and thank-you letters

328
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:37,788
all for Mother's love
for Sir Samuel...

329
00:16:37,872 --> 00:16:39,373
- Volleyball.
- What?

330
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:41,292
Volleyball!

331
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:43,336
[shrieks] Mother!

332
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:47,757
- Good afternoon, ma'am.
- Good afternoon.

333
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:50,551
You look very familiar.

334
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:53,262
But I'm pretty sure I don't know you.

335
00:16:53,513 --> 00:16:56,516
Mother, this is Camille,
Ms. Andrea's new RM.

336
00:16:56,599 --> 00:16:57,767
Ooh...

337
00:16:57,850 --> 00:16:59,060
What's your last name?

338
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:00,186
It's Vergara, ma'am.

339
00:17:06,776 --> 00:17:08,778
[somber music]

340
00:17:26,963 --> 00:17:28,005
[clears throat]

341
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:30,675
We need some candles here.

342
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:32,802
- [Chin] Okay, right away, Mother!
- [Camille] Chin, candles.

343
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:35,805
[Chin] Check the RM's area.
I'll ask Sofie.

344
00:17:43,271 --> 00:17:44,355
[softly] Uh...

345
00:17:45,481 --> 00:17:46,983
Till we meet again, love.

346
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,822
Excuse me, Sir Matthew.

347
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:53,906
- Hey.
- Come here.

348
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:55,616
[Camille] Did I do anything wrong?

349
00:17:56,284 --> 00:17:57,326
Yes.

350
00:17:58,119 --> 00:17:59,245
You're here.

351
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:01,622
But I work here.

352
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:03,374
That's it.

353
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:05,960
There are many jobs out there.

354
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:08,921
I like it here.
I'm not doing this to you on purpose.

355
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:11,215
I know it's difficult.

356
00:18:11,299 --> 00:18:14,135
But I've already
learned so much here.

357
00:18:15,261 --> 00:18:17,680
And I don't know how to explain it.

358
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:21,851
I'm so tired.
I'm hardly getting any sleep.

359
00:18:22,018 --> 00:18:23,269
But I am so happy.

360
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:24,812
I feel so alive.

361
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:27,940
Even if Ms. Andrea yells at me,
I don't mind.

362
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:31,193
Because I want to be as good as her.

363
00:18:32,695 --> 00:18:33,821
As good as you.

364
00:18:42,997 --> 00:18:44,624
Nobody knows about you.

365
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,876
And they don't have to know.

366
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:50,504
I call you Sir Matthew, don't I?

367
00:18:52,632 --> 00:18:54,800
I know showbiz is a small industry.

368
00:18:54,884 --> 00:18:57,053
[in English] We'll have to bump
into each other sometimes.

369
00:18:57,345 --> 00:18:58,429
[in Filipino] I'm fine with it.

370
00:19:00,431 --> 00:19:02,433
[dramatic music]

371
00:19:13,361 --> 00:19:15,029
Camille, let's be clear, people talk.

372
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,990
They can't see us together

373
00:19:20,034 --> 00:19:21,285
or they will find out.

374
00:19:31,754 --> 00:19:34,131
You're smiling
'cause you found the candles, girl?

375
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:39,929
[gasps] Hi, Sir Matthew!

376
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,893
[indistinct chatter]

377
00:19:47,645 --> 00:19:49,897
So how old is your godson?

378
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:52,316
Six, I think. I don't know.

379
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,735
This is only my second gift to him.

380
00:19:54,944 --> 00:19:56,779
The first one was
for their Christening.

381
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:58,030
Oh, Sofie, girl

382
00:19:58,114 --> 00:19:59,657
- you should be ashamed!
- [Sofie chuckles]

383
00:20:00,116 --> 00:20:01,492
[tense music]

384
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:05,246
Sir Gab!

385
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:07,164
[Sofie] What are you doing here,
Sir Gab?

386
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,041
Uh... Checking these, why?

387
00:20:09,125 --> 00:20:11,127
You're supposed to see Joey, right?

388
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:12,962
Oh, right!

389
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:14,046
[Chin] Mm...

390
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:15,131
[Gab] Shoot, here I go again.

391
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,424
- I'll be back soon.
- Wait, Sir Gab.

392
00:20:16,507 --> 00:20:19,593
You can give this to him
to make up for being late again.

393
00:20:19,677 --> 00:20:20,720
- You sure?
- Yes.

394
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:22,054
Thank you.

395
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:24,223
No gift for your poor godson, then.

396
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:26,434
It's okay, there's always next time.

397
00:20:26,684 --> 00:20:28,686
[tense music continues]

398
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:33,232
[indistinct shouting]

399
00:20:33,441 --> 00:20:34,442
[woman] Bye-bye!

400
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:38,988
Oh, you missed the party!

401
00:20:46,871 --> 00:20:47,872
Hi.

402
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:49,915
Uh... Where's Joey?

403
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:52,793
He's at the bookstore with the nanny.

404
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,336
He got bored waiting.

405
00:20:55,129 --> 00:20:57,423
[Lora] I stayed behind
to wait for you.

406
00:20:57,506 --> 00:20:58,507
[exclaims]

407
00:20:58,841 --> 00:21:00,926
I'm sorry about your boss.

408
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,262
[Lora] Poor guy,
he drowned alone in Germany.

409
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:04,889
- [bubbles burbling]
- [rubber duck squeaks]

410
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:07,183
Huh? He didn't drown.

411
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:08,893
Uh... It was a heart attack.

412
00:21:09,477 --> 00:21:11,228
Can you text the nanny
and tell them to come back?

413
00:21:11,604 --> 00:21:13,647
I can't stay long because
I have to go back to the office

414
00:21:13,731 --> 00:21:15,608
for Samuel's memorial service.

415
00:21:15,858 --> 00:21:17,610
- Please.
- You'll make him come back here

416
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:19,153
just to say goodbye?

417
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:23,824
And you want to ask for extra days
when you can't even do one day?

418
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:28,078
If you add up all the hours you've
spent with Joey since this started

419
00:21:28,454 --> 00:21:30,539
it comes down to only three hours.

420
00:21:31,332 --> 00:21:32,833
[scoffs]

421
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:36,170
Mm... Here's a souvenir.

422
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:37,797
You can get back to the office now.

423
00:21:42,676 --> 00:21:44,678
[dramatic music]

424
00:21:48,808 --> 00:21:49,975
[Kiray] Hi, Sofie!

425
00:21:50,059 --> 00:21:51,852
Hey, Kiray, how are you?

426
00:21:51,936 --> 00:21:52,937
[gasps]

427
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:54,021
I know.

428
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:56,774
It's so sad to hear about Sir Samuel.

429
00:21:57,233 --> 00:21:58,818
Do you know what happened?

430
00:21:58,901 --> 00:22:00,402
Mm-hm. It was cholesterol.

431
00:22:00,486 --> 00:22:01,904
He died of a heart attack.

432
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:02,988
Huh?

433
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:04,949
Why did my mom say it was murder?

434
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:08,369
Huh? No, he wasn't murdered.
Where's your mom anyway?

435
00:22:09,411 --> 00:22:10,538
It's just me today.

436
00:22:10,955 --> 00:22:12,039
Is Uncle Gab here?

437
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:15,584
He stepped out, but he'll be back.

438
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:17,837
I'll just wait. Thank you.

439
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:19,672
- Okay, I'll send it right away.
- [Sofie] Yes, hello?

440
00:22:19,755 --> 00:22:20,756
- Thank you.
- Yes.

441
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:21,841
- Okay.
- Okay, sir.

442
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:24,385
Oh, okay...

443
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:25,511
Kiray!

444
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:27,680
Uncle Matthew!

445
00:22:27,763 --> 00:22:30,766
[Kiray] I'm here for Uncle Gab,
but he's out.

446
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:32,309
- I'm sure he'll be back soon.
- [chuckles]

447
00:22:32,393 --> 00:22:34,562
You can wait for him upstairs.
It's a mess down here.

448
00:22:34,645 --> 00:22:35,980
- Come on.
- Okay, thank you!

449
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:37,606
Your mom's not with you?

450
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:40,901
Uh... Actually,
I ditched her, Uncle Matt.

451
00:22:40,985 --> 00:22:42,236
She thinks I'm at the gym.

452
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:44,405
Why'd you do that?

453
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:46,365
Because she keeps bugging me!

454
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:49,034
She's all, "Why not accept
the Hollywood offer?"

455
00:22:49,118 --> 00:22:50,327
"It's Hollywood!"

456
00:22:51,412 --> 00:22:54,832
So I need to talk to Uncle Gab
about my boobs.

457
00:22:55,416 --> 00:22:56,542
Are they really that small?

458
00:22:57,126 --> 00:22:59,128
[playful music]

459
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:00,212
Um...

460
00:23:05,301 --> 00:23:07,303
[window blinds rattle]

461
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:10,222
What do you want for your career?

462
00:23:10,973 --> 00:23:12,808
I have to ask Mama.

463
00:23:12,892 --> 00:23:13,893
I'm asking you.

464
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:19,648
I'm really enjoying acting.

465
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:22,401
Even when I was a kid...

466
00:23:23,611 --> 00:23:28,449
[Kiray] I loved playing
different characters.

467
00:23:31,535 --> 00:23:33,662
I love comedic roles

468
00:23:33,871 --> 00:23:37,416
and when I have to play the mean girl
or fight someone in a scene

469
00:23:37,499 --> 00:23:41,211
no one gets mad at me
because they know I'm just acting.

470
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:46,717
I've been working since I was a kid.

471
00:23:47,217 --> 00:23:50,262
The things normal kids do

472
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:54,433
like playing outside
and going to school...

473
00:23:55,643 --> 00:23:57,561
I've never experienced any of that.

474
00:23:59,021 --> 00:24:01,649
But I enjoy what I have.
I'm still enjoying myself.

475
00:24:04,735 --> 00:24:05,861
Well, in this industry...

476
00:24:07,404 --> 00:24:08,614
you have to be versatile.

477
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:11,533
If you want to get good roles

478
00:24:12,952 --> 00:24:14,203
you have to be famous.

479
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:17,998
That's all your mom wants for you.

480
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:21,835
And I think that's what you need.

481
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:27,132
[Matthew] For instance,
that Hollywood project.

482
00:24:27,716 --> 00:24:29,635
How many actors your age can say

483
00:24:30,344 --> 00:24:33,138
they've starred in a Hollywood film?

484
00:24:34,765 --> 00:24:36,934
But there's a price to pay for that.

485
00:24:39,770 --> 00:24:40,896
Just like everything else.

486
00:24:41,772 --> 00:24:43,482
At least, for you, it's only surgery.

487
00:24:46,318 --> 00:24:47,653
- [Noemi] Ouch!
- [Sofie] Help me please!

488
00:24:47,736 --> 00:24:49,071
Oh, come on! It's just flowers!

489
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:50,739
- Sir Matthew will look for me.
- No, but...

490
00:24:50,823 --> 00:24:53,033
- [Noemi] He needs me there.
- [Sofie] I need you more, Noemi!

491
00:24:53,117 --> 00:24:55,244
- You can do it. You're a big girl.
- Please!

492
00:24:55,786 --> 00:24:57,329
[Noemi] Camille! Are you busy?

493
00:24:58,080 --> 00:24:59,123
Not so much.

494
00:24:59,373 --> 00:25:01,667
Take this upstairs and read the card.
I'll take care of this.

495
00:25:02,126 --> 00:25:03,794
- Thank you, bye.
- Go, girl.

496
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:06,213
[Noemi] I don't want to be involved
in that.

497
00:25:07,131 --> 00:25:09,925
Yeah, I'm telling you,
if you join Shine

498
00:25:10,134 --> 00:25:11,885
your career will be revitalized.

499
00:25:11,969 --> 00:25:13,762
My god, you aren't even here yet

500
00:25:14,179 --> 00:25:15,723
and we already have plans for you!

501
00:25:15,806 --> 00:25:17,641
What more when you finally move here?

502
00:25:18,934 --> 00:25:20,811
[Andrea] Actually,
there's a perfect role for you

503
00:25:20,894 --> 00:25:22,062
in Juan Makabayan!

504
00:25:22,521 --> 00:25:24,356
Enough of those rom-com movies.

505
00:25:24,606 --> 00:25:26,191
They're old news! They're so passé!

506
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:29,862
Okay, let's set a meeting, like,
around next week? Will that be okay?

507
00:25:30,237 --> 00:25:32,114
Perfect, I'll let my RM Camille

508
00:25:32,448 --> 00:25:34,241
message you or text you
to set the meeting.

509
00:25:34,742 --> 00:25:37,369
Okay. No...
I don't need a charcuterie board.

510
00:25:37,703 --> 00:25:40,914
We'll just make sure we give them
a proper notice, okay?

511
00:25:41,123 --> 00:25:42,583
[in English] Bye, Bea! See you!

512
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:44,501
[in Filipino] What's this doing here?

513
00:25:44,585 --> 00:25:46,920
I said to deliver this to Cassie.
Why is it here?

514
00:25:58,015 --> 00:25:59,641
[sighs] You can...

515
00:26:00,142 --> 00:26:02,269
Place these
with the rest of the flowers.

516
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:04,396
Go!

517
00:26:05,064 --> 00:26:06,356
- Take care!
- [Kiray] Okay, thank you!

518
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:07,441
Bye, Kiray!

519
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:11,737
[Gab] Kiray!

520
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:13,739
- Hi!
- [Kiray] Hey, Uncle Gab!

521
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:16,867
Sorry, I went out
to see my son, Joey.

522
00:26:16,950 --> 00:26:18,869
- What's up? Let's go to my office.
- [gasps]

523
00:26:19,161 --> 00:26:20,287
No need, Uncle Gab!

524
00:26:20,537 --> 00:26:23,165
I just ditched Mom,
sorry I couldn't wait for you.

525
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:24,875
I already spoke with Uncle Matthew.

526
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:27,086
I'll decide about Hollywood soon.

527
00:26:27,169 --> 00:26:29,129
- Bye, Uncle Gab!
- [Gab] But we've decided...

528
00:26:31,173 --> 00:26:32,174
[Matthew] Um...

529
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:33,967
[in English] By today.

530
00:26:34,635 --> 00:26:35,677
I'm sure.

531
00:26:35,761 --> 00:26:37,513
- No, that won't be a problem.
- Matty.

532
00:26:38,639 --> 00:26:40,766
- Uh, I need...
- Can I call you back?

533
00:26:41,475 --> 00:26:42,768
I'll call you back, bye.

534
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:44,269
Yeah?

535
00:26:44,353 --> 00:26:45,604
[in Filipino]
What did you tell Kiray?

536
00:26:45,687 --> 00:26:49,108
Nothing, I just brought her upstairs
to wait for you.

537
00:26:49,191 --> 00:26:50,818
- Ms. Andrea, you need to come down.
- That's all?

538
00:26:50,901 --> 00:26:52,694
Uh... Yeah.

539
00:26:52,778 --> 00:26:56,573
No! And also, I congratulated her
on her big Hollywood break.

540
00:26:56,657 --> 00:26:58,867
In the event that she decides
to get the surgery.

541
00:26:59,827 --> 00:27:04,581
Chin is working extra hard,
searching for projects for Kiray.

542
00:27:04,665 --> 00:27:06,250
In exchange for Hollywood.

543
00:27:06,625 --> 00:27:08,252
We talked about this
in the meeting, right?

544
00:27:08,335 --> 00:27:11,088
[breathing heavily]
Now what are you doing?

545
00:27:11,171 --> 00:27:12,714
Why are you meddling with my talents?

546
00:27:12,798 --> 00:27:14,633
Meddling? This is all for SAM.

547
00:27:14,716 --> 00:27:16,969
Your talents are mine too.

548
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:19,847
That's nonsense and you know it.
Why bother splitting up our talents?

549
00:27:20,139 --> 00:27:22,850
You mean to say, I get a cut
from your talents' earnings?

550
00:27:22,933 --> 00:27:24,309
- Hey!
- Tell me it isn't crazy!

551
00:27:24,393 --> 00:27:25,811
- Wait, no!
- Gabriel, listen to me, okay?

552
00:27:25,894 --> 00:27:27,896
- What's happening here?
- Whatever happens to your talents

553
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:29,815
affects all of SAM.

554
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:32,067
I had to step in!
So how did it become nonsense?

555
00:27:32,151 --> 00:27:33,527
- Wait!
- You didn't need to step in...

556
00:27:33,610 --> 00:27:35,028
- Calm down!
- ...because I told you

557
00:27:35,112 --> 00:27:37,072
- I was already handling it, Matty!
- It's for SAM!

558
00:27:37,156 --> 00:27:39,158
- No, but you're not listening!
- Why're you not listening?

559
00:27:39,241 --> 00:27:40,784
Helen!

560
00:27:40,868 --> 00:27:42,244
Hi!

561
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:44,329
[tense music]

562
00:27:53,213 --> 00:27:54,214
Um...

563
00:27:55,799 --> 00:27:58,427
[in English] Helen, on behalf of...

564
00:27:59,136 --> 00:28:00,679
of Andrea and Gabriel

565
00:28:01,221 --> 00:28:04,433
and the rest
of Shine Artist Management

566
00:28:05,767 --> 00:28:10,564
please accept my deepest
and sincerest condolences.

567
00:28:10,898 --> 00:28:12,733
We're very sorry, Helen.

568
00:28:13,025 --> 00:28:15,402
Your loss is ours too, Helen.

569
00:28:16,987 --> 00:28:18,697
Samuel was like a father to me.

570
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:20,073
Actually, to all of us.

571
00:28:20,157 --> 00:28:23,202
Yeah. He wasn't like a husband to me.

572
00:28:26,038 --> 00:28:28,498
[stutters] You came in very early.

573
00:28:28,582 --> 00:28:30,542
[Andrea in Filipino]
We weren't expecting you until later.

574
00:28:30,626 --> 00:28:31,877
[Helen] I just wanted to find out

575
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:34,213
who organized this memorial service.

576
00:28:40,385 --> 00:28:41,386
Uh...

577
00:28:41,470 --> 00:28:44,973
Well, we didn't want
to bother your family.

578
00:28:45,224 --> 00:28:50,062
Uh, so this is for friends
and colleagues in the industry.

579
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:51,355
Yeah.

580
00:28:53,148 --> 00:28:54,149
[Matthew] Um...

581
00:28:54,691 --> 00:28:56,068
Actually, it was...

582
00:28:57,527 --> 00:28:58,570
Mother Aleta.

583
00:28:58,654 --> 00:28:59,655
[scoffs]

584
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,406
- [Helen] I'm sure.
- And...

585
00:29:01,949 --> 00:29:03,992
Well, speaking of Shine...

586
00:29:04,326 --> 00:29:06,328
Uh... [hesitates]

587
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:08,872
Anytime you want to...

588
00:29:09,623 --> 00:29:10,832
- Go on a tour.
- A tour!

589
00:29:10,916 --> 00:29:12,668
A tour of the office.

590
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:14,294
I don't think you've ever been here.

591
00:29:15,379 --> 00:29:17,631
And, also, at the same time

592
00:29:17,714 --> 00:29:20,509
you can use Samuel's office.

593
00:29:22,719 --> 00:29:24,388
Or any office, for that matter.

594
00:29:24,471 --> 00:29:26,598
I mean, it's totally up to you.

595
00:29:26,682 --> 00:29:28,141
And we'll just take it from there.

596
00:29:28,225 --> 00:29:30,227
Then we can discuss how to split...

597
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:31,812
I mean, the...

598
00:29:31,895 --> 00:29:34,648
How we should distribute
Samuel's talents

599
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:38,068
all of Samuel's talents
among ourselves.

600
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:39,361
Uh... [hesitates]

601
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,905
I think what Matthew's
trying to say is

602
00:29:41,989 --> 00:29:44,992
right now, you have
so much to deal with.

603
00:29:45,075 --> 00:29:46,743
You have to be with your family.

604
00:29:46,827 --> 00:29:49,496
And these are the things
we can discuss in the future.

605
00:29:49,579 --> 00:29:52,332
So you don't have to think
about that...

606
00:29:52,416 --> 00:29:55,502
What the boys are trying
to say is that, you know...

607
00:29:55,585 --> 00:29:57,546
[Andrea] You don't have
to decide tonight.

608
00:29:57,796 --> 00:29:59,381
We can just set a meeting
some other time.

609
00:29:59,464 --> 00:30:01,383
When you're ready,
we can talk about it.

610
00:30:01,466 --> 00:30:02,592
And we're just here.

611
00:30:02,926 --> 00:30:06,430
No, it's okay.
It's good you brought it up.

612
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:10,684
Actually, I was wondering
who would ask that first.

613
00:30:11,727 --> 00:30:13,145
And, Matthew, you're right.

614
00:30:13,645 --> 00:30:15,522
I've meant to visit many times

615
00:30:16,606 --> 00:30:20,819
to find out exactly what it was
that was taking Samuel

616
00:30:22,154 --> 00:30:24,990
away from me and my children.

617
00:30:25,407 --> 00:30:29,369
[Helen] What is it with this place
that he comes home late every night?

618
00:30:29,453 --> 00:30:30,662
If he ever does.

619
00:30:31,330 --> 00:30:34,041
Why do I see more of him

620
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:38,837
in magazines and newspapers?

621
00:30:39,463 --> 00:30:40,964
Why do I wake up

622
00:30:41,757 --> 00:30:45,886
alone and without him by my side?

623
00:30:46,345 --> 00:30:48,013
[in English] Well, you know...

624
00:30:49,389 --> 00:30:52,517
Samuel worked really hard for Shine.

625
00:30:52,976 --> 00:30:54,519
This is like his baby.

626
00:30:55,228 --> 00:30:57,439
I wanted to be part of this.

627
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:02,361
[in Filipino] But he wouldn't let me.

628
00:31:03,153 --> 00:31:04,154
Maybe he didn't want me

629
00:31:05,364 --> 00:31:08,492
to know what he does here...

630
00:31:09,117 --> 00:31:11,119
[in English]
Who he shares his bed with.

631
00:31:11,787 --> 00:31:14,331
I just did everything I was told.

632
00:31:14,790 --> 00:31:17,793
I brought my children up so well.

633
00:31:18,710 --> 00:31:20,420
And I was a good wife.

634
00:31:23,173 --> 00:31:26,176
That's why he spoke fondly of you.

635
00:31:26,385 --> 00:31:27,386
[Helen scoffs]

636
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:29,096
No, he didn't.

637
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:34,142
[exhales sharply]

638
00:31:41,858 --> 00:31:44,820
[in Filipino]
I don't need a tour or a meeting.

639
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:50,450
Don't you know
that Samuel left no will?

640
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:54,913
[in English]
Shine belongs to me and my children.

641
00:31:55,580 --> 00:31:57,707
So as of tonight

642
00:31:57,999 --> 00:32:00,377
Shine Artist Management

643
00:32:01,169 --> 00:32:02,921
is for sale

644
00:32:04,548 --> 00:32:06,508
to the highest bidder.

645
00:32:08,927 --> 00:32:09,928
[staff 1] Guys...

646
00:32:10,011 --> 00:32:12,722
- [crowd screaming]
- [staff 2] Guys, please, quiet!

647
00:32:12,806 --> 00:32:16,685
Quiet, please! Guys, listen, quiet!

648
00:32:16,768 --> 00:32:19,813
This is not a movie premiere
or a fan meet.

649
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:21,565
This is a wake.

650
00:32:21,898 --> 00:32:23,316
A memorial service.

651
00:32:23,567 --> 00:32:26,027
So please, there will be no screaming

652
00:32:26,111 --> 00:32:29,698
or we will call the cops
to disperse you all.

653
00:32:29,906 --> 00:32:32,033
- Do you understand?
- [crowd] Yes, sir.

654
00:32:32,117 --> 00:32:33,410
- Okay.
- Be very quiet.

655
00:32:33,493 --> 00:32:35,036
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

656
00:32:35,120 --> 00:32:37,497
[crowd screaming]

657
00:32:37,581 --> 00:32:39,624
[thrilling music]

658
00:32:39,708 --> 00:32:42,210
- [camera shutter clicking]
- [indistinct shouting]

659
00:33:03,315 --> 00:33:04,774
Hello!

660
00:33:06,610 --> 00:33:07,777
More pictures?

661
00:33:16,328 --> 00:33:17,370
How are you?

662
00:33:17,746 --> 00:33:19,664
- You're late again.
- So what?

663
00:33:20,207 --> 00:33:22,542
You're such a joke.

664
00:33:23,502 --> 00:33:25,086
Look at this.

665
00:33:28,089 --> 00:33:30,091
[inaudible dialogue]

666
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:34,387
[Camille] Hello, good evening.

667
00:33:34,471 --> 00:33:35,805
Sir Matthew is over here.

668
00:33:35,889 --> 00:33:37,098
Oh, it's Laurice.

669
00:33:37,182 --> 00:33:38,225
Sir Matthew.

670
00:33:38,308 --> 00:33:39,684
- Matthew.
- Laurice!

671
00:33:39,768 --> 00:33:41,978
- It's nice to see you.
- Nice to see you.

672
00:33:42,062 --> 00:33:46,024
Mr. E, Mr. C, Laurice.

673
00:33:46,107 --> 00:33:47,234
Yeah, and, of course...

674
00:33:47,317 --> 00:33:48,318
Yes?

675
00:33:48,401 --> 00:33:50,153
- Excuse me.
- Okay.

676
00:33:51,154 --> 00:33:52,781
Camille, just a minute.

677
00:33:54,533 --> 00:33:55,951
Malou, I hope you don't mind.

678
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:57,619
Camille, this is Malou Crisologo.

679
00:33:57,702 --> 00:33:59,704
Line producer for Juan Makabayan.

680
00:34:00,247 --> 00:34:03,375
And these two fine gentlemen here

681
00:34:03,458 --> 00:34:06,545
are the producers
of that monumental film.

682
00:34:06,795 --> 00:34:09,339
- This is Mr. E and Mr. C.
- Nice to meet you. Hello.

683
00:34:09,422 --> 00:34:11,049
Malou, this is Camille.

684
00:34:11,132 --> 00:34:14,010
- She's Andrea's new RM.
- Okay.

685
00:34:14,094 --> 00:34:17,222
Okay, she just finished film school.
And she's so used to being on set.

686
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:19,641
Perfect. Perfect timing!

687
00:34:19,724 --> 00:34:24,104
Because I am doing five movies
all at the same time.

688
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:25,981
It's giving me a headache.

689
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:27,774
Mr. E here is all paid up.

690
00:34:27,857 --> 00:34:29,359
But we still don't have a location!

691
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:30,944
Sorry about that, Mr. E.

692
00:34:31,027 --> 00:34:33,738
We've been to Spain so many times.

693
00:34:33,822 --> 00:34:35,782
But we won't go over budget.

694
00:34:35,865 --> 00:34:37,242
Uh... [nervous chuckle]

695
00:34:37,325 --> 00:34:39,869
How about TV? Do you also do TV work?

696
00:34:39,953 --> 00:34:40,954
Because I also have...

697
00:34:41,830 --> 00:34:44,082
- I'm not really looking...
- No, of course she does!

698
00:34:44,165 --> 00:34:45,625
- Not just TV and movies.
- Good!

699
00:34:45,709 --> 00:34:46,960
And even commercials.

700
00:34:47,043 --> 00:34:48,086
- Good.
- Not to worry.

701
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:50,171
- I'll send you her contact details.
- Yes.

702
00:34:50,255 --> 00:34:52,132
- Yes, I'm on Facebook. ASAP, please.
- Thank you, Lou!

703
00:34:52,215 --> 00:34:54,342
- Mr. E, Mr. C.
- [Sofie] My name is Sofie Lasola.

704
00:34:54,426 --> 00:34:58,471
If you're looking for a new actress,
you can watch my play.

705
00:34:59,723 --> 00:35:02,058
Okay, Sofie, thank you.

706
00:35:02,767 --> 00:35:03,935
- Ma'am Aleta.
- Mm?

707
00:35:04,269 --> 00:35:05,270
Um...

708
00:35:05,353 --> 00:35:07,939
Now I want you to meet
two stalwarts of the industry.

709
00:35:09,024 --> 00:35:12,569
This beautiful lady is none other
than Ms. Roselle Monteverde

710
00:35:12,652 --> 00:35:13,820
- from Regal Films.
- I'm Camille.

711
00:35:13,903 --> 00:35:15,071
- This is Camille.
- Hello, ma'am.

712
00:35:15,155 --> 00:35:17,699
And this good-looking
gentleman right here

713
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:19,242
is none other than

714
00:35:19,326 --> 00:35:20,785
- Mr. Vincent del Rosario...
- Hello.

715
00:35:20,869 --> 00:35:21,995
...of Viva Films.

716
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:23,997
- Hello, sir.
- You've got in one room

717
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:26,541
Regal Films and Viva Films.

718
00:35:26,625 --> 00:35:27,626
You can choose to be

719
00:35:28,293 --> 00:35:31,046
a Regal Baby or a Viva Hot Babe.

720
00:35:31,796 --> 00:35:33,923
- [all laugh]
- Matthew.

721
00:35:34,507 --> 00:35:36,343
Hello, hi, nice to see you.

722
00:35:36,426 --> 00:35:37,677
- Mr. Vincent.
- Hello, how are you?

723
00:35:37,761 --> 00:35:38,803
Uh...

724
00:35:38,887 --> 00:35:40,347
- [Gab] Mother.
- Gabriel.

725
00:35:40,430 --> 00:35:41,890
Excuse me.

726
00:35:45,518 --> 00:35:47,270
Here. Thanks anyway.

727
00:35:47,562 --> 00:35:49,814
Why didn't you give it to Joey?

728
00:35:50,607 --> 00:35:51,608
Uh...

729
00:35:51,941 --> 00:35:52,984
He already had one.

730
00:35:54,819 --> 00:35:55,820
Oh...

731
00:35:55,904 --> 00:35:57,614
This is my gift to you.

732
00:35:58,657 --> 00:35:59,658
Thank you.

733
00:36:01,743 --> 00:36:03,745
[ominous music]

734
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:18,718
My condolences, Matthew.

735
00:36:19,552 --> 00:36:20,595
[cell phone beeps]

736
00:36:22,055 --> 00:36:24,057
[indistinct chatter]

737
00:36:27,977 --> 00:36:29,979
[ominous music continues]

738
00:36:36,569 --> 00:36:37,570
Excuse me.

739
00:36:38,238 --> 00:36:39,239
Excuse me.

740
00:36:40,281 --> 00:36:41,449
- Hi.
- Hi.

741
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:46,162
Excuse me.

742
00:36:47,038 --> 00:36:50,417
Helen, I'm Paul Amir.

743
00:36:50,500 --> 00:36:53,837
[Paul] And I'm really,
really sorry...

744
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:55,922
[indistinct chatter]

745
00:37:00,802 --> 00:37:04,556
I hope there will be an opportunity
for us to talk sometime.

746
00:37:04,639 --> 00:37:06,683
- Maybe over a cup of coffee?
- Excuse me. Helen?

747
00:37:07,559 --> 00:37:08,727
- Paul.
- Yes?

748
00:37:09,018 --> 00:37:10,687
I'll be back, okay?

749
00:37:13,273 --> 00:37:15,275
[ominous music intensifies]

750
00:37:18,945 --> 00:37:19,946
[both gasp]

751
00:37:20,029 --> 00:37:21,573
[in English] I'm so sorry.

752
00:37:21,656 --> 00:37:23,116
- It's okay!
- I'm so sorry.

753
00:37:23,199 --> 00:37:24,325
Did I hurt you?

754
00:37:24,409 --> 00:37:26,286
- No, it's okay.
- I'm sorry I ruined your flowers.

755
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:27,996
It's okay. I'm fine, no worries.

756
00:37:28,329 --> 00:37:29,330
Um...

757
00:37:29,706 --> 00:37:32,208
I'm Rina, by the way,
if you need anything.

758
00:37:33,293 --> 00:37:35,587
Okay. I'll take note of that. Andrea.

759
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:36,921
[in Filipino]
What are you doing here?

760
00:37:37,756 --> 00:37:40,008
[in English]
Paying my respects, of course.

761
00:37:40,091 --> 00:37:42,010
[in Filipino]
It's a good turnout, right?

762
00:37:42,302 --> 00:37:43,803
[in English]
Well, Samuel was very well-loved.

763
00:37:43,887 --> 00:37:47,056
Oh, yes. I just met his wife, Helen.

764
00:37:47,640 --> 00:37:49,309
[in Filipino]
I heard she's selling something.

765
00:37:49,893 --> 00:37:50,935
Am I right, Matthew?

766
00:37:55,190 --> 00:37:56,649
[in English] I'm sorry again, ma'am.

767
00:37:56,733 --> 00:37:57,734
It's okay.

768
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:02,530
Uh...

769
00:38:02,947 --> 00:38:04,199
Matthew.

770
00:38:06,743 --> 00:38:07,952
[in Filipino] That's not yet final.

771
00:38:10,121 --> 00:38:11,289
Really?

772
00:38:13,041 --> 00:38:16,836
But Helen sounded so sure.

773
00:38:16,920 --> 00:38:18,880
You still don't believe me, do you?

774
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:23,384
That, without Samuel,
Shine is going nowhere but down.

775
00:38:29,933 --> 00:38:30,934
Paul.

776
00:38:32,352 --> 00:38:34,312
If you think that Shine is worthless

777
00:38:36,564 --> 00:38:37,649
why are you buying it?

778
00:38:38,942 --> 00:38:42,737
And if Samuel is the only reason
for its success

779
00:38:43,238 --> 00:38:44,489
why are you offering me a job?

780
00:38:44,739 --> 00:38:46,115
- [in English] Sorry, again.
- It's okay.

781
00:38:47,742 --> 00:38:50,620
[Paul in Filipino]
Because you're good at your job.

782
00:38:50,703 --> 00:38:53,373
For all you know,
you might be the next Samuel.

783
00:38:53,581 --> 00:38:57,585
It doesn't matter who buys Shine.

784
00:38:57,669 --> 00:39:01,673
After all, I think that will help
with the transition.

785
00:39:02,799 --> 00:39:07,887
They'll only buy it for the name,
then afterwards, close it down.

786
00:39:09,639 --> 00:39:10,849
I'm still thinking about it.

787
00:39:13,643 --> 00:39:16,938
[in English] I'm not sure
I can do that to Andrea and Gabriel.

788
00:39:20,525 --> 00:39:21,901
Matthew.

789
00:39:23,778 --> 00:39:25,154
[in Filipino] You may shine...

790
00:39:26,406 --> 00:39:27,740
but we are the galaxy.

791
00:39:30,243 --> 00:39:34,080
Do you want to be with them
so far down the ladder of success?

792
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:39,127
- [Noemi] Sir Matthew...
- [Daisy] Idol! Picture, please!

793
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:40,628
[Noemi] Sir Matthew?

794
00:39:41,170 --> 00:39:43,089
- [Daisy] Thank you.
- [Noemi] Where's Sir Matthew?

795
00:39:43,673 --> 00:39:44,841
Over here, guys.

796
00:39:45,300 --> 00:39:46,301
Sir Matthew.

797
00:39:46,384 --> 00:39:47,719
Matt!

798
00:39:47,802 --> 00:39:49,470
- [Matthew] I'll call you.
- [Noemi] Sir Matthew.

799
00:39:49,554 --> 00:39:50,972
Brandon and Jessica are here.

800
00:39:51,055 --> 00:39:53,099
- [Matthew] Jess!
- [Jessica] Hey, Matthew.

801
00:39:53,182 --> 00:39:55,393
- How are you? Good to see you.
- [Matthew] So nice to see you, hi!

802
00:39:55,476 --> 00:39:56,769
- Brandon, buddy!
- How are you?

803
00:39:56,853 --> 00:39:57,854
[Brandon] Good to see you!

804
00:39:58,605 --> 00:40:00,815
[rock music]

805
00:40:03,151 --> 00:40:04,444
[Brandon laughs]

806
00:40:04,527 --> 00:40:05,778
- Good to see you!
- [Matthew] Yeah.

807
00:40:05,862 --> 00:40:06,988
Good to see you too.

808
00:40:07,906 --> 00:40:09,407
[in English]
I'd like you to meet some people.

809
00:40:09,490 --> 00:40:10,825
- Yes, sir. Yeah.
- [Matthew] Okay.

810
00:40:10,909 --> 00:40:14,078
This is one of our country's most
talented singers and actresses

811
00:40:14,162 --> 00:40:15,246
Ms. Zsa Zsa Padilla.

812
00:40:15,330 --> 00:40:17,081
- Nice to meet you.
- [Brandon] Zsa Zsa, how are you?

813
00:40:17,165 --> 00:40:19,083
[Matthew] And her equally
talented daughter, Karylle.

814
00:40:19,167 --> 00:40:20,710
Hi, Karylle. Nice to meet you!

815
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:23,504
And Samuel's widow, Helen.

816
00:40:24,255 --> 00:40:26,716
Condolences, Mrs. Mendiola.

817
00:40:29,510 --> 00:40:32,472
[Brandon] Ma'am, the world lost
a good man in Samuel.

818
00:40:33,306 --> 00:40:36,142
I promise he's going to be missed.
That's for sure.

819
00:40:36,225 --> 00:40:39,604
We also heard about what happened.

820
00:40:39,687 --> 00:40:42,190
For us, we wanna make sure
that'll never happen to you.

821
00:40:42,649 --> 00:40:44,901
We want to make sure that you could
always protect yourself.

822
00:40:45,652 --> 00:40:46,819
So we got you this.

823
00:40:47,862 --> 00:40:50,365
I know how classy you are,
Mrs. Mendiola.

824
00:40:50,448 --> 00:40:54,035
So we got this for you,
just from Texas.

825
00:40:55,036 --> 00:40:56,329
[in Filipino] It's beautiful!

826
00:40:56,412 --> 00:40:57,914
- [in English] It looks nice!
- And deadly!

827
00:40:59,123 --> 00:41:01,584
[nervous chuckle]
Brandon, I need a minute.

828
00:41:01,668 --> 00:41:02,752
Okay.

829
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:04,295
- [Matthew] Excuse us.
- Excuse me.

830
00:41:05,755 --> 00:41:08,049
[Helen] Will someone
please take this off me?

831
00:41:08,716 --> 00:41:09,801
[Niño] Hi, ma'am!

832
00:41:09,884 --> 00:41:12,136
Your ex and I had a movie together.

833
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:13,471
[chuckles] Mr. Director!

834
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:15,556
[romantic music]

835
00:41:22,397 --> 00:41:24,148
[in English] Ma'am, your drink.

836
00:41:24,691 --> 00:41:26,609
But I didn't ask for a drink.

837
00:41:27,110 --> 00:41:29,278
I just wanted to say
you have beautiful eyes.

838
00:41:30,405 --> 00:41:31,406
Uh...

839
00:41:31,864 --> 00:41:33,866
By the way,
this is my personal number.

840
00:41:33,950 --> 00:41:36,119
Please call me directly
if you need anything.

841
00:41:36,452 --> 00:41:37,537
Yeah, sure, I'll...

842
00:41:37,996 --> 00:41:39,038
Thank you.

843
00:41:39,122 --> 00:41:40,832
Thank you. Have a good night.

844
00:41:42,291 --> 00:41:43,292
Bye.

845
00:41:50,550 --> 00:41:52,969
Maricel, Snooky, just in time.

846
00:41:53,511 --> 00:41:54,721
[in Filipino] This way.

847
00:41:54,804 --> 00:41:56,806
[thrilling music]

848
00:42:17,076 --> 00:42:18,327
Let's get on with the meeting.

849
00:42:18,411 --> 00:42:19,495
Wait a second.

850
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:21,914
[whimsical music]

851
00:42:28,755 --> 00:42:29,797
Okay.

852
00:42:33,176 --> 00:42:35,470
[Gab] Chin, look for Director Mac.

853
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:36,929
- Oh!
- [Andrea] Hi! Hello!

854
00:42:37,430 --> 00:42:38,431
Um...

855
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:39,515
Hello.

856
00:42:39,599 --> 00:42:41,267
[in English] Ms. Helen

857
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:42,769
I would like you
to meet our biggest stars

858
00:42:42,852 --> 00:42:45,146
Ms. Maricel Soriano
and Ms. Snooky Serna.

859
00:42:45,229 --> 00:42:47,732
Of course, I know them very well.

860
00:42:48,107 --> 00:42:52,779
[in Filipino] Who doesn't know
these huge movie stars?

861
00:42:53,237 --> 00:42:54,697
[Helen] And I know

862
00:42:54,906 --> 00:42:57,158
Samuel worked on both of you
at the same time.

863
00:42:57,867 --> 00:42:59,494
I mean...

864
00:42:59,994 --> 00:43:02,163
on both of your careers, of course.

865
00:43:03,706 --> 00:43:06,626
Actually, we're meeting
for a new project.

866
00:43:06,709 --> 00:43:08,795
[in English]
So if you don't mind, excuse us.

867
00:43:08,878 --> 00:43:10,797
- Let's go? Let's go.
- Let's go.

868
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:12,507
Did you get the bag that I sent you?

869
00:43:13,299 --> 00:43:16,010
[in Filipino] Yes, Ms. Jessica.
I got it. Thank you.

870
00:43:16,803 --> 00:43:17,804
[Noemi] Come in.

871
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:22,809
[in English] I heard a rumor

872
00:43:24,268 --> 00:43:25,311
about Samuel.

873
00:43:26,646 --> 00:43:27,814
[in Filipino] That he got shot.

874
00:43:28,022 --> 00:43:29,023
[Matthew] Fake news.

875
00:43:29,107 --> 00:43:30,358
He was on a date with Madel

876
00:43:31,567 --> 00:43:32,819
when he had a heart attack.

877
00:43:34,737 --> 00:43:37,198
I'll be outside.
And thanks again, Ms. Jessica!

878
00:43:39,325 --> 00:43:40,326
[door closes]

879
00:43:40,952 --> 00:43:42,620
[Matthew in English]
Hey, we're not doing that!

880
00:43:42,703 --> 00:43:43,871
Noemi.

881
00:43:44,247 --> 00:43:45,373
Yes, sir?

882
00:43:45,456 --> 00:43:48,126
[in Filipino] Can you hand me
their advertising contracts

883
00:43:48,209 --> 00:43:50,837
for Thorade and Manila Mansion,
please?

884
00:43:50,920 --> 00:43:51,963
[in English] Right away, sir.

885
00:43:52,046 --> 00:43:53,047
[door closes]

886
00:43:53,756 --> 00:43:54,799
[door opens]

887
00:43:55,800 --> 00:43:56,884
[Matthew] Thank you!

888
00:44:00,596 --> 00:44:01,681
[door closes]

889
00:44:01,764 --> 00:44:03,432
[Jessica] Get off of me, okay?

890
00:44:03,516 --> 00:44:05,017
Do you want me
to divorce you right now?

891
00:44:05,101 --> 00:44:06,269
[Brandon in Filipino] Try it!

892
00:44:06,352 --> 00:44:07,979
Let's see if you can
afford this lifestyle.

893
00:44:08,062 --> 00:44:09,313
Do you have a prenup?

894
00:44:09,397 --> 00:44:10,398
Where is it?

895
00:44:10,690 --> 00:44:11,691
Whip it out!

896
00:44:12,191 --> 00:44:14,902
No prenup, no discussions, okay?

897
00:44:15,236 --> 00:44:17,822
[in Filipino] I never wished
for anything bad on anyone.

898
00:44:18,823 --> 00:44:19,824
You know that.

899
00:44:22,201 --> 00:44:23,494
I'm not a bad person.

900
00:44:24,620 --> 00:44:25,955
But my reputation was ruined.

901
00:44:27,331 --> 00:44:30,001
Is it my fault that my performance

902
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:31,711
had the greater impact?

903
00:44:32,461 --> 00:44:34,714
That I am the better actor?

904
00:44:36,966 --> 00:44:38,217
I'm the one who was wronged.

905
00:44:39,135 --> 00:44:40,344
I'm the one who was maligned.

906
00:44:42,013 --> 00:44:45,183
I am the victim.

907
00:44:45,266 --> 00:44:46,809
- Idiot.
- What the heck?

908
00:44:46,893 --> 00:44:47,894
[Andrea chuckles]

909
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:49,520
What?

910
00:44:49,687 --> 00:44:51,230
Oh, dear. She called me an idiot.

911
00:44:51,314 --> 00:44:54,358
Did you hear that, Gabriel?
See how this woman treats me?

912
00:44:54,442 --> 00:44:55,443
Oh...

913
00:44:55,526 --> 00:44:59,030
Why would I want to work
with someone like that?

914
00:44:59,322 --> 00:45:02,283
And what makes you think
I want to be anywhere with you?

915
00:45:02,366 --> 00:45:04,660
If there was one movie left
in the universe

916
00:45:04,744 --> 00:45:08,247
I wouldn't do it
if you're in it with me, humph!

917
00:45:08,331 --> 00:45:12,126
You're so scared people will see
that I have more awards!

918
00:45:12,210 --> 00:45:15,004
[Snooky] You're not
that good of an actor anyway.

919
00:45:15,087 --> 00:45:16,672
- You're just jealous!
- Oh, no.

920
00:45:16,756 --> 00:45:19,258
You want everything that I have!

921
00:45:19,342 --> 00:45:22,595
[Maricel] Title roles, houses,
everything!

922
00:45:22,678 --> 00:45:24,972
- Even Samuel! Right?
- [gasps]

923
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:26,933
I'm sorry to break your hearts

924
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:29,060
but there will be no divorce.

925
00:45:29,852 --> 00:45:31,812
Thorade ends 2027.

926
00:45:32,521 --> 00:45:33,731
Three commercials per year.

927
00:45:34,190 --> 00:45:37,109
Manila Mansion, 2030.

928
00:45:38,277 --> 00:45:40,071
- [Brandon] Oh, no.
- Four commercials per year.

929
00:45:40,154 --> 00:45:41,989
[Matthew] It's stipulated
in both contracts

930
00:45:42,073 --> 00:45:43,324
that you cannot divorce.

931
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:45,826
Divorce means breach of contract.

932
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:49,163
We know that.
We've been playing house long enough.

933
00:45:50,164 --> 00:45:51,249
We can wait.

934
00:45:51,707 --> 00:45:52,792
Well there you go!

935
00:45:53,251 --> 00:45:55,044
[in English]
But after these two contracts

936
00:45:55,127 --> 00:45:57,255
we don't want any more
couple endorsements.

937
00:45:57,338 --> 00:45:59,257
[Jessica] We just want solo contracts
from now on.

938
00:45:59,340 --> 00:46:01,008
Please, please...

939
00:46:01,592 --> 00:46:04,553
So I don't have to look at this thing
even at work.

940
00:46:04,971 --> 00:46:07,098
[Matthew] Okay,
this is the bottom line.

941
00:46:07,181 --> 00:46:09,267
No one can know
that you want a divorce

942
00:46:09,350 --> 00:46:13,354
and no one can definitely know
why you even want one.

943
00:46:13,813 --> 00:46:14,814
Wait a minute.

944
00:46:16,524 --> 00:46:17,650
Why do you want a divorce, anyway?

945
00:46:18,567 --> 00:46:20,027
Well? Tell him why.

946
00:46:20,111 --> 00:46:23,656
You have a personal "trainer," right?

947
00:46:23,739 --> 00:46:25,157
- [Brandon] In that gym?
- [mouths] Shut up.

948
00:46:25,241 --> 00:46:27,535
I wonder what you're training for.

949
00:46:28,119 --> 00:46:29,578
He's your boyfriend, isn't he?

950
00:46:29,996 --> 00:46:30,997
Ha?

951
00:46:31,080 --> 00:46:32,123
Am I right?

952
00:46:32,665 --> 00:46:34,500
[in English]
I'm a woman and I have needs.

953
00:46:34,583 --> 00:46:38,212
I understand that during fight camps,
we can't do it.

954
00:46:38,754 --> 00:46:41,048
But what about outside
of fight camps?

955
00:46:41,340 --> 00:46:43,426
I still don't get any!

956
00:46:44,051 --> 00:46:45,344
I'm just being careful!

957
00:46:45,720 --> 00:46:46,846
[in Filipino] What if I go weak?

958
00:46:47,555 --> 00:46:48,597
I don't want to get sick!

959
00:46:49,015 --> 00:46:51,142
Samuel loved me first, Mary!

960
00:46:51,225 --> 00:46:53,477
- Don't you call me Mary!
- There you go.

961
00:46:53,561 --> 00:46:54,562
Not now, not ever!

962
00:46:55,563 --> 00:46:58,983
You would visit Samuel
every single day!

963
00:46:59,066 --> 00:47:01,110
Just because you know he liked me!

964
00:47:01,193 --> 00:47:02,194
[Maricel] That's what it was!

965
00:47:02,278 --> 00:47:03,404
[Snooky] You have it all wrong!

966
00:47:03,487 --> 00:47:06,157
He was visiting me every day
because he was in love with me!

967
00:47:06,240 --> 00:47:08,659
[Maricel] No, you're wrong!

968
00:47:08,743 --> 00:47:11,037
- You went to him every day!
- [Snooky] No...

969
00:47:11,120 --> 00:47:13,748
Okay, ladies.

970
00:47:14,081 --> 00:47:16,709
We don't care how big Sam's penis is.

971
00:47:16,792 --> 00:47:19,045
We have to talk about the project!
We're going off-track here.

972
00:47:19,128 --> 00:47:20,963
- We sure are!
- Are we really going off-track?

973
00:47:21,047 --> 00:47:22,631
- Yes, we are way off-track!
- Yes.

974
00:47:22,965 --> 00:47:24,383
You have to do this film!

975
00:47:24,467 --> 00:47:25,718
- I agree!
- You two are the reigning

976
00:47:25,801 --> 00:47:27,803
Queens of Philippine Cinema!

977
00:47:27,887 --> 00:47:30,097
[Matthew in English] Okay, guys.
This is what's going to happen.

978
00:47:30,181 --> 00:47:32,683
Jessica and your fitness instructor

979
00:47:33,726 --> 00:47:34,727
are no more.

980
00:47:34,810 --> 00:47:36,187
You're never gonna
see each other again.

981
00:47:36,270 --> 00:47:38,064
[in Filipino]
You have to step out of this room

982
00:47:38,147 --> 00:47:41,067
looking like you are still in love.

983
00:47:41,359 --> 00:47:42,860
You will always hold hands.

984
00:47:43,444 --> 00:47:44,445
[in English] Come on!

985
00:47:45,446 --> 00:47:46,781
Come on, Brandon, come on!

986
00:47:46,864 --> 00:47:48,240
[in Filipino]
You will always be kissing.

987
00:47:50,034 --> 00:47:51,077
Come on.

988
00:47:51,535 --> 00:47:52,536
[groans]

989
00:47:52,620 --> 00:47:54,497
And of course,
you will be all over each other.

990
00:47:54,580 --> 00:47:55,790
[grunts]

991
00:47:57,958 --> 00:48:00,628
Even before you step out,
they should start feeling it already.

992
00:48:01,295 --> 00:48:03,297
[in English]
Come on, give me a smile!

993
00:48:03,798 --> 00:48:06,217
Come on!

994
00:48:07,009 --> 00:48:08,052
Come on, Brandon!

995
00:48:08,135 --> 00:48:09,929
No, you give me your smile.

996
00:48:10,012 --> 00:48:11,222
You give me your smile!

997
00:48:11,305 --> 00:48:13,057
Get out of here! Come on!

998
00:48:13,682 --> 00:48:15,518
You lovely couple, you.

999
00:48:15,601 --> 00:48:18,479
Come on, there you go.

1000
00:48:18,562 --> 00:48:22,942
Imagine, two of the greatest actors
of this generation

1001
00:48:23,025 --> 00:48:26,821
in one historic film,
just imagine it!

1002
00:48:27,446 --> 00:48:30,157
[Andrea] Streaming services
will be fighting over this.

1003
00:48:30,366 --> 00:48:33,119
A Snooky Serna-Maricel Soriano movie.

1004
00:48:33,786 --> 00:48:35,746
Maricel Soriano as Paula

1005
00:48:35,830 --> 00:48:38,791
and Snooky Serna as Candida.
Perfection!

1006
00:48:38,874 --> 00:48:39,959
- And...
- Perfection!

1007
00:48:40,042 --> 00:48:41,627
- Wait.
- [Andrea] What?

1008
00:48:41,710 --> 00:48:42,711
Uh...

1009
00:48:42,795 --> 00:48:43,963
It's Snooky as Paula.

1010
00:48:44,338 --> 00:48:46,215
- No.
- [Gab] Maricel as Candida.

1011
00:48:46,298 --> 00:48:47,341
Yes.

1012
00:48:47,425 --> 00:48:49,009
- [Andrea] Gab, we agreed on this.
- Right, yes!

1013
00:48:49,093 --> 00:48:52,763
I said Maricel is perfect for Paula

1014
00:48:52,847 --> 00:48:54,181
and you agreed with me.

1015
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:56,308
No, I agreed they were perfect for it

1016
00:48:56,600 --> 00:48:59,228
but it has always been
Snooky as Paula!

1017
00:48:59,311 --> 00:49:01,814
- Gab, you got it wrong again.
- No, I'm Paula!

1018
00:49:01,897 --> 00:49:03,482
I thought you knew how to compromise!

1019
00:49:03,566 --> 00:49:05,317
This is probably why Cassie left you!

1020
00:49:05,651 --> 00:49:08,362
Hey, Gabriel Anthony Soler!

1021
00:49:08,446 --> 00:49:11,115
- You want to make this personal?
- But I really didn't...

1022
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:13,701
Your wife left you because
you always go back on your word!

1023
00:49:13,784 --> 00:49:17,288
- I'm just trying to prove a point!
- I said Maricel is Paula!

1024
00:49:17,371 --> 00:49:19,457
- That's not what we talked about!
- She's the only one for it.

1025
00:49:19,540 --> 00:49:21,542
- We agreed Snooky is Paula!
- You agreed with me. No!

1026
00:49:21,625 --> 00:49:23,502
[clamoring]

1027
00:49:23,586 --> 00:49:24,628
Ms. Andrea!

1028
00:49:24,712 --> 00:49:26,797
Director Mac is here!

1029
00:49:26,881 --> 00:49:28,299
[Andrea] Who was first, huh?
Between us?

1030
00:49:28,382 --> 00:49:30,217
Please move, everyone!

1031
00:49:30,301 --> 00:49:31,469
Hold on, Sir Matthew.

1032
00:49:31,552 --> 00:49:33,888
- They're in an acting workshop.
- A workshop...

1033
00:49:33,971 --> 00:49:35,514
What kind?

1034
00:49:35,598 --> 00:49:37,475
- [chuckles]
- Stanislavsky? Adler?

1035
00:49:37,558 --> 00:49:39,894
- [Helen] Until the very end...
- Morris?

1036
00:49:39,977 --> 00:49:42,730
Shine has done nothing
but embarrass me.

1037
00:49:43,856 --> 00:49:44,940
Bye, Matthew.

1038
00:49:46,066 --> 00:49:49,737
Don't be fooled
by a smooth-sailing production.

1039
00:49:50,779 --> 00:49:55,701
If a film gets made with no problems,
it will flop.

1040
00:49:56,619 --> 00:50:01,165
But if it's problematic and messy

1041
00:50:02,082 --> 00:50:05,252
then that's a sure box-office hit!

1042
00:50:24,563 --> 00:50:25,606
[in English] What a day, huh?

1043
00:50:30,152 --> 00:50:31,862
[in Filipino]
I know you didn't like it

1044
00:50:32,821 --> 00:50:34,657
when I introduced you to producers.

1045
00:50:37,159 --> 00:50:39,119
[in English]
I just wanted to give you options.

1046
00:50:40,538 --> 00:50:41,830
[in Filipino] I'm good here.

1047
00:50:43,040 --> 00:50:44,041
You're here.

1048
00:50:52,091 --> 00:50:53,217
[in English] You know, Camille...

1049
00:50:54,635 --> 00:50:55,803
I grew up here.

1050
00:50:57,846 --> 00:50:59,223
[Matthew] Samuel was my mentor.

1051
00:51:02,309 --> 00:51:03,352
And now he's gone.

1052
00:51:05,062 --> 00:51:07,106
[in Filipino] But there's a lot more
for me out there.

1053
00:51:08,524 --> 00:51:11,110
And I'm not sure if SAM can keep up.

1054
00:51:17,283 --> 00:51:18,867
You have so many secrets, huh?

1055
00:51:21,579 --> 00:51:22,955
I'm sure you have your reasons

1056
00:51:23,038 --> 00:51:26,208
but if I don't know
what you're going through

1057
00:51:26,292 --> 00:51:29,128
or why you're keeping
those secrets...

1058
00:51:30,629 --> 00:51:32,006
I really can't help you.

1059
00:51:37,845 --> 00:51:38,929
I just want you to know

1060
00:51:39,013 --> 00:51:40,639
that I didn't want
to mess up your life.

1061
00:51:42,766 --> 00:51:45,102
You said we can't be seen together.

1062
00:51:46,604 --> 00:51:47,605
I said, that's fine.

1063
00:51:49,857 --> 00:51:51,609
But Ms. Andrea hired me.

1064
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:54,903
I figured maybe the universe
did it for me.

1065
00:51:55,571 --> 00:51:58,032
If we can't be father and daughter

1066
00:51:59,658 --> 00:52:00,993
we can still be together somehow.

1067
00:52:04,663 --> 00:52:06,749
My dream somehow came true.

1068
00:52:10,085 --> 00:52:11,128
Come on.

1069
00:52:12,171 --> 00:52:14,590
- I'll drive you home.
- Okay.

1070
00:52:18,093 --> 00:52:19,094
Let's go.

1071
00:52:23,057 --> 00:52:25,059
[somber music]

1072
00:52:47,456 --> 00:52:48,457
[Matthew] Gab.

1073
00:52:49,667 --> 00:52:50,709
What's your problem?

1074
00:52:50,793 --> 00:52:51,835
You're my problem.

1075
00:52:52,378 --> 00:52:54,129
[in English] Stay away from Kiray,
let me handle it.

1076
00:52:54,588 --> 00:52:56,215
[in Filipino]
I'm just trying to help.

1077
00:52:56,507 --> 00:52:58,884
Don't worry, Gab.
Matthew won't bother you anymore.

1078
00:52:58,967 --> 00:53:01,970
He won't meddle with Kiray because
he's too busy sucking up to Helen.

1079
00:53:02,054 --> 00:53:03,305
I'm not talking to you either.

1080
00:53:03,389 --> 00:53:05,808
[sarcastic chuckle]
Oh, wow. You're mad at me?

1081
00:53:05,891 --> 00:53:08,227
- Who brought up Cassie?
- Excuse me.

1082
00:53:08,310 --> 00:53:10,813
Not another scene.
I've had it with both of you.

1083
00:53:11,730 --> 00:53:14,692
Hello, Laurice. Sorry, I know.

1084
00:53:14,775 --> 00:53:16,819
- [Andrea] Hi. Let's go in?
- I know.

1085
00:53:16,902 --> 00:53:20,572
[Madel crying] Why, Samuel, why?

1086
00:53:20,656 --> 00:53:23,534
[wailing]

1087
00:53:23,617 --> 00:53:24,618
Why?

1088
00:53:26,912 --> 00:53:27,996
Samuel...

1089
00:53:29,164 --> 00:53:30,874
Why?

1090
00:53:30,958 --> 00:53:32,960
[sobbing]

1091
00:53:37,548 --> 00:53:38,590
Who is this?

1092
00:53:39,341 --> 00:53:40,509
It's Madel.

1093
00:53:41,301 --> 00:53:45,514
[Aleta] She's tried so many times,
but she still hasn't reached the urn.

1094
00:53:47,015 --> 00:53:50,477
Just because
she was with him in Germany

1095
00:53:50,561 --> 00:53:52,938
doesn't mean she can act like this.

1096
00:53:53,021 --> 00:53:58,402
Why can't she be as quiet
as Samuel's other mistresses here?

1097
00:53:58,861 --> 00:53:59,945
Which ones are they?

1098
00:54:03,282 --> 00:54:06,660
You see that woman over there,
with the veil?

1099
00:54:07,911 --> 00:54:09,455
- That's Rowena.
- [Andrea] Mm-hm.

1100
00:54:10,330 --> 00:54:12,833
That one, near the urn?

1101
00:54:12,916 --> 00:54:14,168
Mm?

1102
00:54:14,251 --> 00:54:16,211
- [Aleta] That's Grace.
- [Andrea] Mm-hm.

1103
00:54:16,795 --> 00:54:18,964
This one behind me on the left.

1104
00:54:19,047 --> 00:54:22,134
- Don't look. I said, don't look.
- Mm-hm.

1105
00:54:23,469 --> 00:54:24,553
That one is Chiqui.

1106
00:54:25,679 --> 00:54:31,643
Further back, two rows away,
is Sabel.

1107
00:54:32,936 --> 00:54:38,942
- The other one over there is Bambi.
- Mm-hm.

1108
00:54:42,946 --> 00:54:43,989
Who else?

1109
00:54:44,698 --> 00:54:48,243
See that one?
The one with the flower on her head.

1110
00:54:49,369 --> 00:54:50,829
- [Aleta] See her?
- [Andrea] Yeah.

1111
00:54:50,913 --> 00:54:52,372
That's Cynthia.

1112
00:54:53,624 --> 00:54:55,125
And... [clears throat]

1113
00:54:57,961 --> 00:54:58,962
You okay?

1114
00:55:00,047 --> 00:55:01,048
Of course.

1115
00:55:01,298 --> 00:55:02,466
I've been okay for a while now.

1116
00:55:05,385 --> 00:55:06,762
[sighs]

1117
00:55:08,430 --> 00:55:09,431
[Aleta] Wait.

1118
00:55:09,515 --> 00:55:10,724
Mm?

1119
00:55:10,808 --> 00:55:14,144
What happened
between you three earlier?

1120
00:55:14,228 --> 00:55:15,270
[exasperated sigh]

1121
00:55:15,979 --> 00:55:17,481
[in English] It's a hopeless project.

1122
00:55:18,398 --> 00:55:21,652
[in Filipino]
Everyone wants the Paula role.

1123
00:55:22,444 --> 00:55:24,780
Maricel and Snooky hate each other.

1124
00:55:24,863 --> 00:55:26,448
So, it's a no-go.

1125
00:55:26,907 --> 00:55:28,492
[in English]
It's really... It's hopeless.

1126
00:55:28,575 --> 00:55:29,618
It's not gonna happen.

1127
00:55:29,701 --> 00:55:30,702
Andrea!

1128
00:55:31,161 --> 00:55:32,621
[in Filipino]
What do you mean it's hopeless?

1129
00:55:33,288 --> 00:55:35,082
Don't ever think it's hopeless.

1130
00:55:35,999 --> 00:55:38,126
Let me handle Maricel and Snooky.

1131
00:55:39,002 --> 00:55:40,420
What you need to fix

1132
00:55:40,504 --> 00:55:43,340
is all this fighting
amongst you managers.

1133
00:55:43,757 --> 00:55:44,925
You can't carry on that way.

1134
00:55:45,843 --> 00:55:47,553
You have to end it soon.

1135
00:55:48,720 --> 00:55:52,808
Samuel will roll in his grave,
I tell you.

1136
00:55:57,396 --> 00:56:00,065
Okay, I'm going to take a walk.

1137
00:56:00,691 --> 00:56:02,943
I've seen this movie already.

1138
00:56:04,820 --> 00:56:06,822
[somber music]

1139
00:56:12,494 --> 00:56:14,496
[indistinct dialogue]

1140
00:56:19,710 --> 00:56:21,712
[somber music continues]

1141
00:56:55,662 --> 00:56:58,624
[somber music continues]

1142
00:57:16,475 --> 00:57:18,060
[thunder rumbles]

1143
00:57:18,143 --> 00:57:19,186
[Matthew] Take care.

1144
00:57:19,269 --> 00:57:21,271
[rain pattering]

1145
00:57:35,619 --> 00:57:37,663
They say rain means blessings.

1146
00:57:40,499 --> 00:57:42,084
You know what, Matthew, you're right.

1147
00:57:44,419 --> 00:57:46,630
We need to have a plan for SAM.

1148
00:57:49,341 --> 00:57:51,134
Okay. Let's figure it out.

1149
00:57:52,010 --> 00:57:54,429
So, with your permission

1150
00:57:55,180 --> 00:57:56,765
I'll let the other RMs know.

1151
00:57:56,848 --> 00:58:00,811
They can get everything ready
for this planning session.

1152
00:58:02,437 --> 00:58:03,438
Of course.

1153
00:58:10,278 --> 00:58:11,321
Hi, Uncle Gab.

1154
00:58:16,118 --> 00:58:17,160
Kiray?

1155
00:58:17,244 --> 00:58:18,286
[Gab] I can call Kelly.

1156
00:58:19,538 --> 00:58:23,375
She said we could
change our minds, so...

1157
00:58:23,709 --> 00:58:25,919
I'm sure she'll be glad
you're taking it.

1158
00:58:27,713 --> 00:58:28,714
I just hope

1159
00:58:29,548 --> 00:58:33,719
she forgives me for yelling at her.

1160
00:58:34,344 --> 00:58:35,387
And I'm sorry.

1161
00:58:35,679 --> 00:58:37,472
Why are you apologizing, Uncle Gab?

1162
00:58:37,556 --> 00:58:40,183
I feel that I didn't protect you.

1163
00:58:41,727 --> 00:58:42,853
I was no help to you at all.

1164
00:58:43,186 --> 00:58:44,271
I'm good!

1165
00:58:45,147 --> 00:58:46,982
This will be helpful to me.

1166
00:58:47,649 --> 00:58:48,984
Oh, think of it this way.

1167
00:58:49,735 --> 00:58:52,029
This will boost my confidence

1168
00:58:52,404 --> 00:58:54,948
and inspire me to work harder.

1169
00:58:55,365 --> 00:58:56,575
Listen to me.

1170
00:58:57,117 --> 00:58:59,244
Your career
isn't the only important thing.

1171
00:58:59,327 --> 00:59:00,328
You're still young.

1172
00:59:00,620 --> 00:59:02,664
[in English]
You should be enjoying yourself.

1173
00:59:03,290 --> 00:59:05,542
[in Filipino]
I am enjoying myself, Uncle Gab.

1174
00:59:07,377 --> 00:59:08,628
[Kiray] I really want to do this.

1175
00:59:08,962 --> 00:59:13,300
Because of this,
I can make more films.

1176
00:59:13,800 --> 00:59:15,302
I really love this.

1177
00:59:15,761 --> 00:59:16,887
Thank you!

1178
00:59:16,970 --> 00:59:18,972
[laughs]

1179
00:59:19,056 --> 00:59:20,432
Thanks, God!

1180
00:59:20,515 --> 00:59:22,642
[Mrs. Celis] This rain won't let up.

1181
00:59:23,310 --> 00:59:24,311
Mommy?

1182
00:59:25,896 --> 00:59:27,272
[in English] Freebie.

1183
00:59:29,107 --> 00:59:30,317
Wow, Gab.

1184
00:59:31,777 --> 00:59:33,820
We're going to Holy Wood!

1185
00:59:34,279 --> 00:59:36,490
Yeah, Hollywood!

1186
00:59:36,573 --> 00:59:37,616
Holy Wood!

1187
00:59:37,699 --> 00:59:38,950
- Holy Wood!
- Yes, Hollywood!

1188
00:59:39,034 --> 00:59:41,036
[whimsical music]

1189
00:59:43,413 --> 00:59:44,831
Mm!

1190
00:59:44,915 --> 00:59:46,166
Michael, this is too salty.

1191
00:59:46,249 --> 00:59:47,709
Add some water.

1192
00:59:48,085 --> 00:59:49,127
Will do.

1193
00:59:50,962 --> 00:59:52,255
Are they here?

1194
00:59:52,672 --> 00:59:54,299
- [cook] Order, Table 6.
- [server] Copy.

1195
00:59:54,382 --> 00:59:55,967
[Aleta] It's Maria. Mm!

1196
00:59:57,260 --> 00:59:58,428
Hello!

1197
00:59:58,512 --> 00:59:59,888
[over speaker] Still no Cookie?

1198
01:00:00,847 --> 01:00:02,933
How can anyone be late
for a Zoom call?

1199
01:00:05,060 --> 01:00:06,061
[gasps]

1200
01:00:06,895 --> 01:00:09,189
[notification beeps]

1201
01:00:09,731 --> 01:00:12,859
Mother, where is Maria?

1202
01:00:12,943 --> 01:00:15,153
[Snooky] I thought we had a meeting.

1203
01:00:15,779 --> 01:00:18,031
Mother, you know I hate waiting.

1204
01:00:22,452 --> 01:00:24,704
God, these two. Hold it up higher!

1205
01:00:24,788 --> 01:00:25,872
[assistant] Yes, Mother.

1206
01:00:25,956 --> 01:00:27,457
[notification beeps]

1207
01:00:27,999 --> 01:00:29,209
Still not here?

1208
01:00:29,793 --> 01:00:31,878
Am I supposed to wait for her?

1209
01:00:33,588 --> 01:00:37,008
Are you sure we need Mary here
in the meeting?

1210
01:00:37,092 --> 01:00:40,262
Mother personally invited me, hello.

1211
01:00:40,345 --> 01:00:42,139
You know, you two...

1212
01:00:42,931 --> 01:00:47,060
In America,
they call this an intervention.

1213
01:00:47,477 --> 01:00:50,522
[Aleta] But here in the Philippines,
we call it

1214
01:00:50,605 --> 01:00:55,235
"I'll knock you both senseless
if you don't fix this mess."

1215
01:00:55,318 --> 01:00:56,528
- [gasps]
- [flame roars]

1216
01:00:56,611 --> 01:00:58,071
What was that, Michael?

1217
01:00:58,738 --> 01:00:59,739
Okay.

1218
01:01:00,115 --> 01:01:01,950
Let me ask you this.

1219
01:01:02,576 --> 01:01:09,875
Who produced Underage and Schoolgirls

1220
01:01:09,958 --> 01:01:13,003
and all the films
that made you famous?

1221
01:01:13,378 --> 01:01:14,713
- You did.
- You did.

1222
01:01:14,796 --> 01:01:17,799
[Aleta] Mm! Hey, Michael.

1223
01:01:18,216 --> 01:01:19,968
The squash is excellent!

1224
01:01:20,051 --> 01:01:22,345
- Make this again!
- [Michael] Yes, ma'am.

1225
01:01:23,096 --> 01:01:26,725
Who paid for your debts

1226
01:01:26,808 --> 01:01:30,562
when you squandered your earnings

1227
01:01:30,645 --> 01:01:33,064
from those movies?

1228
01:01:33,481 --> 01:01:34,733
- You did.
- You did.

1229
01:01:34,816 --> 01:01:39,613
And who do you thank for everything?

1230
01:01:40,363 --> 01:01:42,407
- First, God.
- I want to thank you.

1231
01:01:42,490 --> 01:01:46,036
- [Snooky] My family. And...
- [Maricel] The production.

1232
01:01:46,119 --> 01:01:50,540
- And... Samuel, Andrea.
- Samuel, Gab.

1233
01:01:50,624 --> 01:01:54,211
- And then, of course, Shine.
- My mom and dad.

1234
01:01:54,294 --> 01:01:57,297
- Okay, I get it.
- [Snooky] Right, Mother?

1235
01:01:57,839 --> 01:01:59,216
We'll do it this way.

1236
01:02:01,134 --> 01:02:04,471
The Portrait of An Artist
as a Filipino.

1237
01:02:05,180 --> 01:02:06,431
You're both doing it.

1238
01:02:07,432 --> 01:02:09,059
[Aleta] Maricel, how old are you?

1239
01:02:09,893 --> 01:02:11,019
Fifty-four.

1240
01:02:11,102 --> 01:02:12,687
How about you, Snooky?

1241
01:02:12,771 --> 01:02:14,022
Fifty-three.

1242
01:02:14,689 --> 01:02:16,650
Maria, you'll play Paula.

1243
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:18,818
Snooky, you are Candida.

1244
01:02:19,694 --> 01:02:20,737
Period.

1245
01:02:20,820 --> 01:02:23,073
Think of your fans, okay?

1246
01:02:24,241 --> 01:02:26,201
When we're all dead and gone

1247
01:02:26,326 --> 01:02:30,497
they will remember you,
they will never forget you

1248
01:02:30,580 --> 01:02:33,250
because of this film.

1249
01:02:34,751 --> 01:02:36,044
So do it.

1250
01:02:36,378 --> 01:02:37,420
Yes, ma'am.

1251
01:02:37,504 --> 01:02:40,632
[ringing]

1252
01:02:40,715 --> 01:02:44,344
Hey, Rey! How's my piano?

1253
01:02:45,971 --> 01:02:47,973
[piano key plays]

1254
01:02:53,478 --> 01:02:54,980
Nice!

1255
01:02:55,063 --> 01:02:57,399
[Mac] I'm really excited.
Everything's set.

1256
01:02:57,899 --> 01:03:00,402
Just the small matter of billing.

1257
01:03:01,611 --> 01:03:03,697
Yes, and I go first, right?

1258
01:03:05,365 --> 01:03:07,117
Here we go again.

1259
01:03:07,909 --> 01:03:08,910
[Snooky] Oh?

1260
01:03:09,786 --> 01:03:11,496
I'm an award-winning actress.

1261
01:03:11,871 --> 01:03:13,999
All my films make money.

1262
01:03:14,082 --> 01:03:16,167
[Maricel] So if I get top billing

1263
01:03:16,251 --> 01:03:19,170
this movie will make money.

1264
01:03:19,254 --> 01:03:21,047
If not, that won't happen.

1265
01:03:23,008 --> 01:03:25,343
Are we doing this for the critics?

1266
01:03:25,427 --> 01:03:27,804
If they're the only ones
who'll watch, then why do it at all?

1267
01:03:29,264 --> 01:03:30,348
Maricel.

1268
01:03:30,890 --> 01:03:34,227
[Snooky] You got the part you wanted

1269
01:03:34,728 --> 01:03:37,897
so I should get
the billing I deserve!

1270
01:03:38,148 --> 01:03:39,274
Director, hold this for me please.

1271
01:03:39,357 --> 01:03:40,400
Okay.

1272
01:03:40,483 --> 01:03:42,402
- How are we...
- I've had it. I've really had it.

1273
01:03:43,028 --> 01:03:44,738
- [Snooky] Now she's upset?
- Pass this to Sir Gab.

1274
01:03:44,821 --> 01:03:46,573
She stole my role,
now she wants to steal my billing.

1275
01:03:46,656 --> 01:03:49,242
[Maricel] Because that's the only way
to get people to watch this movie.

1276
01:03:49,326 --> 01:03:50,952
- Pass this to Sir Gab.
- She wants to get her way

1277
01:03:51,036 --> 01:03:52,454
- even though it's clear...
- From Camille.

1278
01:03:52,537 --> 01:03:53,663
...that I deserve top billing.

1279
01:03:53,747 --> 01:03:56,624
- [Maricel] Oh, don't kid yourself.
- Sir Gab.

1280
01:03:56,708 --> 01:03:59,002
We all know who the true star is.

1281
01:03:59,085 --> 01:04:01,254
[Snooky] And we all know
who the better actress is.

1282
01:04:01,338 --> 01:04:03,381
Delusional is what you are.

1283
01:04:03,465 --> 01:04:05,717
[Maricel] And you?
You're out of your mind!

1284
01:04:05,800 --> 01:04:07,469
[Snooky] Let's see your awards then!

1285
01:04:07,552 --> 01:04:11,681
Actually, I think Camille
has a solution here.

1286
01:04:12,307 --> 01:04:13,558
Can you explain?

1287
01:04:14,309 --> 01:04:15,560
Uh...

1288
01:04:15,643 --> 01:04:19,564
The graphics will be a circle

1289
01:04:19,647 --> 01:04:22,984
turning constantly like this.

1290
01:04:23,068 --> 01:04:25,153
Your names will be in the circle

1291
01:04:25,236 --> 01:04:28,990
so no one is on top or the bottom.

1292
01:04:29,366 --> 01:04:32,118
Then we can create separate

1293
01:04:32,202 --> 01:04:34,954
social media pages.

1294
01:04:36,247 --> 01:04:39,167
And separate posters.

1295
01:04:39,250 --> 01:04:42,420
[Noemi] One for Paula
and one for Candida.

1296
01:04:45,757 --> 01:04:49,636
[film rolling]

1297
01:04:51,471 --> 01:04:53,556
Fantastic! Yes!

1298
01:04:55,767 --> 01:04:58,895
[Mac in English] I love it! Love it.

1299
01:04:59,604 --> 01:05:02,107
Love it. It's nice, right, Maricel?

1300
01:05:02,816 --> 01:05:03,858
Back to you.

1301
01:05:05,652 --> 01:05:06,903
And back to you.

1302
01:05:09,656 --> 01:05:11,324
[Mac] We need to do
an ocular ASAP, okay?

1303
01:05:11,408 --> 01:05:14,285
- The interiors are very important.
- [Aleta] It went very well.

1304
01:05:14,369 --> 01:05:17,622
- [Aleta] Thank you!
- [Mac] Thank you!

1305
01:05:17,747 --> 01:05:20,500
- Bye!
- Take care!

1306
01:05:20,583 --> 01:05:23,628
Oh, I love you. It's so cute!

1307
01:05:23,711 --> 01:05:25,672
- [overlapping dialogue]
- [dog barking]

1308
01:05:25,755 --> 01:05:28,591
[exhales sharply] Congratulations!

1309
01:05:28,675 --> 01:05:32,178
- Your kids are very smart!
- Of course!

1310
01:05:32,262 --> 01:05:34,681
Everyone in SAM is smart!

1311
01:05:35,014 --> 01:05:37,767
Agree. Okay, I'm going!

1312
01:05:37,892 --> 01:05:39,477
- Thank you so much, Mother!
- Bye, Mother!

1313
01:05:39,561 --> 01:05:40,687
Thank you.

1314
01:05:40,979 --> 01:05:42,647
- Bye!
- [Gab] Take care!

1315
01:05:43,773 --> 01:05:45,900
- [Andrea] Bye, Mother!
- [Aleta] Bye-bye!

1316
01:05:45,984 --> 01:05:47,235
- Bye, Mother.
- Bye-bye!

1317
01:05:47,318 --> 01:05:48,778
- See you!
- [Maricel] Thank you.

1318
01:05:53,491 --> 01:05:55,577
Something's wrong with this one.

1319
01:05:55,660 --> 01:05:56,703
Oh...

1320
01:05:56,786 --> 01:05:58,163
Is this my dog?

1321
01:05:58,246 --> 01:05:59,414
I should go.

1322
01:05:59,497 --> 01:06:01,082
- Bye-bye!
- Bye!

1323
01:06:01,166 --> 01:06:02,625
[relieved sigh]

1324
01:06:02,709 --> 01:06:04,961
- So?
- [Andrea] I think we have a project!

1325
01:06:05,753 --> 01:06:06,796
Good job.

1326
01:06:06,880 --> 01:06:09,591
[Gab] I didn't think it was possible,
but they finally agreed on something.

1327
01:06:09,674 --> 01:06:10,967
- [Sofie] Ms. Andrea.
- [Andrea] What?

1328
01:06:12,427 --> 01:06:13,470
What is it?

1329
01:06:17,307 --> 01:06:18,349
[Andrea] Oh, no.

1330
01:06:18,433 --> 01:06:19,559
[shudders]

1331
01:06:19,642 --> 01:06:22,896
- [moaning]
- [notifications pinging]

1332
01:06:22,979 --> 01:06:23,980
My god.

1333
01:06:24,939 --> 01:06:25,940
Noemi.

1334
01:06:26,024 --> 01:06:27,942
- No...
- My god.

1335
01:06:28,026 --> 01:06:30,028
[closing theme music]
